{
  "slug": "big-tempeh-oat-breakfast-bowl",
  "name": "Big tempeh and savoury oat breakfast bowl",
  "description": "Rolled oats simmered savoury in unsweetened soy milk, piled with browned tempeh, mushrooms, broccoli and spinach — a large protein-forward breakfast bowl built for a high morning calorie target on plants alone.",
  "iconKey": "bowl",
  "instructions": [
    "Bring the soy milk to a simmer in a wide pan, stir in the rolled oats and the salt, and cook for 5 minutes until thick.",
    "Meanwhile cube the tempeh and brown it in a dry non-stick pan over medium-high heat for 4 minutes, turning once.",
    "Add the sliced mushrooms and the broccoli florets to the tempeh, cover the pan and cook for 4 minutes, until the broccoli is bright and just tender.",
    "Fold the spinach through the pan off the heat and season with the black pepper.",
    "Spoon the oats into a large bowl and pile the tempeh, mushrooms, broccoli and spinach on top."
